{
"about": "Real (after inflation) total returns for each calendar year, January to January: US stocks (the S&P 500 and its predecessors, price change plus the year's dividends) and US government bonds (a 10-year bond bought at the January long rate and valued a year later at the new rate, plus its coupon). Worked out from Robert Shiller's monthly data. Used only to replay history against a plan (js/lifetime/stress.js); it is the past, not a forecast.",
